  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Vulnerabilities of Refugees and Third-Country Nationals in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration (IOM) proposes this intervention to address the protection and social cohesion needs of Ukrainian refugees, Third-Country Nationals (TCNs), and vulnerable residents of hosting communities in the Republic of Moldova. The proposed project is aligned with the Regional Refugee Response Plan (RRRP) and IOM&#x2019;s mid-term strategy for Moldova. It was developed in coordination with national and local authorities as part of the ongoing work under the National Referral Mechanism for Victims of Crime (NRMV), and will support the operationalization of IOM&#x2019;s Area-Based Approach (ABA) in targeted communities. Activities underlying the Outcome 1 result statement were designed to support the realization of NRMV Specific Objectives &#x2013; a set of concrete Government priorities building on almost a decade of IOM&#x2019;s technical assistance. Social Cohesion activities and the resulting output underlying Outcome 2 were developed in coordination with local authorities, IOM&#x2019;s in-country partners, and local civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
